---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import PageIntro from '../components/PageIntro.astro';
import CtaBand from '../components/CtaBand.astro';
import { PHONE, TEL_HREF, STEPS } from '../data/site';
import { serviceSchema } from '../data/schema';

const title = 'Mobile European Auto Repair Services | Eway Auto Repairs';
const description = `European auto repair at your driveway in South Jersey: diagnostics, scheduled maintenance, brakes, coding, second opinions and pre-purchase inspections. 30+ years, ASE Master certified. Call ${PHONE}.`;

const schemas = [
  serviceSchema(
    'Mobile European Auto Repair',
    'Mobile diagnostics, maintenance, and repair for European cars in South Jersey.',
    '/services'
  ),
];

const detailed = [
  {
    anchor: 'svc-diagnostics',
    num: '01',
    title: 'Diagnostics',
    paras: [
      'Check engine lights, intermittent faults, electrical gremlins, and the problems another shop gave up on. I run factory-level scan capability — full-module access, live data, guided tests — not a generic code reader from the parts store.',
      'A fault code is where diagnosis starts, not where it ends. The code tells you which circuit complained; thirty years on these platforms tells you which part on your specific engine actually causes that complaint. That difference is why I fix cars other shops throw parts at.',
    ],
  },
  {
    anchor: 'svc-maintenance',
    num: '02',
    title: 'Scheduled Maintenance',
    paras: [
      'Oil and filters, brake fluid, coolant, spark plugs, belts, transmission services — done to the manufacturer schedule with the correct approved fluids. European engines are specific about oil approvals, and "close enough" is how engines sludge up.',
      'I also service the things the maintenance display pretends do not exist: the "lifetime" transmission fluids, the Haldex couplings, the brake fluid nobody flushes. The cars that reach 200k are the ones that got these done.',
    ],
  },
  {
    anchor: 'svc-brakes',
    num: '03',
    title: 'Brakes & Suspension',
    paras: [
      'Pads, rotors, wear sensors, control arms, bushings, struts, and sway bar links — correct parts, correct torque, correct procedure. Modern European cars need their electronic parking brakes retracted and reset with a scan tool, and wear sensors replaced, not bent out of the way.',
      'On suspension I tell you what is actually worn versus what a lift-and-shake inspection flags to pad an estimate. Bushings crack cosmetically long before they fail functionally; you will get the honest version.',
    ],
  },
  {
    anchor: 'svc-coding',
    num: '04',
    title: 'Coding & Programming',
    paras: [
      'Module coding, adaptations, retrofits, and service resets that most independent shops cannot touch. Battery registration on BMWs, component protection on VW-Audi, injector coding, feature enabling — the software side of a modern European car is half the job.',
      'This matters most after a repair: a new battery, module, or component often needs to be introduced to the car properly, or you inherit electrical gremlins that get blamed on everything else.',
    ],
  },
  {
    anchor: 'svc-second',
    num: '05',
    title: 'Second Opinions',
    paras: [
      'Got a dealer quote that doesn’t feel right? Bring it to me. I’ll look at the car, tell you what it actually needs, what can safely wait, and what on the quote is padding.',
      'Most of the time the repair is smaller than what was quoted. Sometimes it isn’t — and then you at least know the big quote is real before you spend it.',
    ],
  },
];
---

<Page title={title} description={description} path="/services" schemas={schemas}>
  <PageIntro eyebrow="Services">
    <Fragment slot="title">What I do in your <span class="accent">driveway</span>.</Fragment>
    <Fragment slot="intro">
      Diagnostics, maintenance, and repair for European cars — at your home or workplace,
      anywhere in the South Jersey service area. Written estimate before any work, itemized
      invoice after.
    </Fragment>
  </PageIntro>

  <section class="section-ruled">
    <div class="section container">
      {
        detailed.map((s, i) => (
          <div id={s.anchor} class:list={['svc-block']} style={i > 0 ? 'margin-top:64px' : ''}>
            <div class="eyebrow" data-reveal>{s.num}</div>
            <h2 data-reveal>{s.title}</h2>
            <div class="copy">
              {s.paras.map((p) => (
                <p>{p}</p>
              ))}
            </div>
          </div>
        ))
      }

      <div id="ppi-overview" style="margin-top:64px">
        <div class="eyebrow" data-reveal>06</div>
        <h2 data-reveal>Pre-Purchase Inspections</h2>
        <div class="copy">
          <p>
            Buying a used European car? I inspect it before you commit — at the seller's
            location. Full module scan, mechanical inspection, photos, and a straight answer on
            whether to buy. The cheapest money you'll ever spend on a car.
          </p>
          <p>
            <a href="/pre-purchase-inspection">Everything that's included in a PPI →</a>
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="next-links">
        <a class="chip-link" href="/pre-purchase-inspection">Pre-Purchase Inspection</a>
        <a class="chip-link" href="/brands">Brands I work on</a>
        <a class="chip-link" href="/service-area">Service area</a>
        <a class="chip-link" href="/contact">Request a quote</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-alt">
    <div class="section container">
      <div class="eyebrow" data-reveal>How It Works</div>
      <h2 data-reveal>Four steps, no surprises.</h2>
      <div class="step-grid">
        {
          STEPS.map((st) => (
            <div class="step" data-reveal>
              <div class="numeral">{st.n}</div>
              <h3>{st.title}</h3>
              <p>{st.body}</p>
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </div>
      <div class="copy" style="margin-top:44px">
        <p>
          That process isn't marketing — it's how New Jersey says auto repair should work, and
          it's how I've always worked: a written estimate before anything is taken apart,
          written authorization, and an itemized invoice separating parts and labor. Call
          <a href={TEL_HREF}>{PHONE}</a> and it starts with a conversation, not a commitment.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CtaBand />
</Page>
